  "brief": "<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> Market Overview</h2>\n\nMixed signals in pre-market with a clear defensive rotation underway. Tech bleeding with QQQ down 1.02% while Healthcare leads at +3.01%, suggesting institutional money is moving to safety. VIX cooling to 24.07 indicates some complacency, but this sector divergence screams caution.\n\n<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> What to Watch</h2>\n\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Initial Jobless Claims (12:30 ET)</strong> - Labor market data could shift Fed expectations with multiple employment metrics hitting simultaneously</li>\n<li><strong>Fed Barkin Speech (12:30 ET)</strong> - Timing with jobs data makes this critical for rate trajectory signals</li>\n<li><strong>Nonfarm Productivity Final (12:30 ET)</strong> - Inflation implications if productivity disappoints while labor costs surge</li>\n<li><strong>Tech Sector Weakness</strong> - XLK down 2.49% needs to hold key support or broader market follows</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> Sector Rotation</h2>\n\nClassic risk-off rotation with Healthcare (XLV +3.01%) and Financials (XLF +2.20%) leading while Tech gets hammered. This isn't random - smart money positioning for economic uncertainty or rate environment shifts. Energy barely red despite Iran supply concerns suggests demand destruction fears outweigh geopolitics.\n\n<div class=\"callout callout-green\"><div class=\"callout-label\">✦ Bull Case</div>Healthcare strength suggests institutional rotation, not broad selling. Small caps (IWM +0.91%) outperforming indicates domestic growth optimism intact.</div>\n\n<div class=\"callout callout-red\"><div class=\"callout-label\">⚠ Bear Case</div>Tech weakness spreading could trigger broader tech selloff. VIX at 24 means any surprise from jobs data or Fed speech amplifies volatility.</div>\n\n<div class=\"callout callout-amber\"><div class=\"callout-label\">⚡ Key Driver</div>12:30 ET data dump with jobs claims, productivity, and Fed speech simultaneously could whipsaw markets in either direction.</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> Levels That Matter</h2>\n\n<ul>\n<li><strong>SPY 750</strong> - Critical support, break below opens 740 gap fill</li>\n<li><strong>QQQ 730</strong> - Must hold or tech rout accelerates</li>\n<li><strong>XLK 185</strong> - Sector support level, break triggers broader tech selling</li>\n<li><strong>VIX 26</strong> - Break above signals fear escalation, defensive positioning warranted</li>\n</ul>\n\n<hr>\n<p><em>Not a prediction. A preparation. Make your plan before the bell.</em></p>",
